### Media Upload Flow (Zero-Server-Load Pipeline)
1. **Request Ticket**: Client sends image dimensions (width, height, mimeType, fileSizeBytes) to POST /api/v1/media/upload-ticket.
2. **Pre-Signed Generation**: Backend validates upload rules, generates an immutable S3 storage key (uploads/{user_id}/{ulid}.webp), and produces a 15-minute cryptographically signed AWS S3 PUT URL.
3. **Direct Binary Push**: Client uploads binary image directly to Object Storage via HTTP PUT.
4. **Instant BlurHash & Ingestion**: Frontend computes lightweight BlurHash string on-canvas or backend worker verifies header and anchors BlurHash in PostgreSQL. Server memory never consumes high-resolution image streams.

